{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the children of Israel, and Elohim knew.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): because Israel were in Egypt enslaved in crushing labor, afflicted with all kinds of divergent troubles one from another, and the Egyptians schemed to harm them and devised against them in this, sometimes openly and sometimes in secret — therefore Scripture says, וירא אלהים, concerning the troubles that the Egyptians inflicted upon them openly, which were visible to the eye; and וידע אלהים, concerning the troubles that they inflicted upon them in secret, which were not known to any creature but to HaShem, blessed be He, alone, for He is the one who knows and is witness." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: וידע אלהים and וירא אלהים — I have already explained it, and it is like the matter of (Numbers 6:25) ״יאר יהוה פניו אליך״, and וידע אלהים is from the matter of the Tree of Knowledge, for an influx is drawn from the Rachamim (Mercy) to the Da'at (Knowledge) to have compassion upon Israel. And so you will find in Sefer ha-Bahir: What is וידע אלהים? To what may the matter be likened? To a king who had a wife and established sons from her; he cherished them and raised them, and they went astray. As it is said, ״ושנא אמם״ — their mother returned to them and said, 'My sons, why are you like this? Your father hates me and you' — until they returned to do the will of their father. Their father saw this and loved them as at first, and remembered their mother. Of this it is written: וירא וידע. End quote. And of this it is said (Proverbs 10:1–2): ״ובן כסיל תוגת אמו״ — and not 'his father,' because his mother is distant from his father on his account. And from here is a clear proof: all the while Israel are in exile, the influx and the emanation is cut off from the Chariot and the light of the Countenance is distant from the Da'at, and then the children are exiled; and when they return in repentance, He draws His compassion to the Da'at and loves the children as at first, and then the children are redeemed — and this is what is mentioned here: וירא וידע, and through this they were redeemed. And this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:29.902727579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}